Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: SC2 stateful VP9/AVS2 and depth-correct scatter DRM PRIME

Register AVS2 in the actual configure, codec and object tables and split VP9
superframes before handing complete coded frames to the stateful decoder.
The AVS2 fourcc and AMF8/AMF0 capture formats are the local native SC2 ABI.

Preserve negotiated compressed fourccs rather than round-tripping logical
YUV through a linear format. Export the actual decoder-owned object size,
fd and dequeued header offset. AMF8 is eight-bit scatter with MEM_SAVING;
AMF0 is ten-bit scatter without MEM_SAVING. Both use the negotiated aligned
width as DRM pitch; neither is CPU-linear YUV. Existing Request decoders,
including their AMF0 path, are not modified.

Validate FBC sizes using negotiated padded capture geometry, and reallocate
native surfaces when actual depth, allocation layout or unpadded COMPOSE
dimensions change, even when the padded capture dimensions remain equal.

An optional video_device decoder option lets Kodi pin its capability-probed
native node; the existing autodetection remains the default.

